.override.yml`. Audits in this container\n> are therefore not reproducible from tracked files alone.\n\n## 1. Project identity\n\nA Docker-packaged coding-agent environment wrapping the OpenCode binary around a\nDeepSeek \"V4.1 Flash\" provider plus Jev review/guard tooling, managed via Dockge.\n\n- **`README.txt`** — prerequisites: Docker Engine, authenticated `gh`, a DeepSeek key\n  (`sk-`, platform.deepseek.com/api_keys), a Jev key (`apikey_`,\n  console.typesafe.ai/keys). Keys cached in `../.env.local` (mode 0600, gitignored).\n- **`QUICKSTART.txt`** — `cd scripts && ./deploy-dockge.sh`, then\n  `./flatten-dockge-stacks.sh`, then open `http://localhost:5001`.\n- **`opencode.json`** — provider `deepseek` (`@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`,\n  `baseURL https://api.deepseek.com`, `apiKey {env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}`); model\n  `deepseek-flash` (context 1,000,000 / output 384,000); `\"plugin\": [\"jev-guard\"]`;\n  `\"skills\": [\"/opt/jev-review/skills\"]`; MCP server `jev-review` =\n  `node /opt/jev-review/dist/server.js` with `JEV_API_KEY`.\n- **`docker/Dockerfile`** — `node:22-bookworm-slim`, xdg-open no-op shim, installs\n  OpenCode, installs `jev-guard@0.3.1 --global`, clones `NiazMorshed2007/jev-review`\n  to `/opt/jev-review` pinned at `3fb6042ebf07f0fdaae30d65c6393848e1a549e3`.\n\n## 2. Rule system\n\n```\n$ grep -rhoE \"#[0-9]+\" /workspace/notes --include=\"*.txt\" | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -30\n    390 #5\n     50 #8\n     42 #12\n     38 #9\n     32 #13\n     28 #7\n     20 #14\n     13 #3\n     12 #54\n     11 #1\n      9 #55\n      9 #53\n      8 #45\n      8 #39\n      8 #10\n      7 #5604\n      7 #34\n      7 #2\n      6 #6\n      6 #57\n      6 #41\n      6 #4\n      6 #38\n      6 #37\n      6 #18\n      6 #17\n      6 #11\n      5 #47\n      5 #15\n      4 #16\n```\n\n**The top-30 is dominated by Docker BuildKit step markers, not rule references.** Of\n**779 total `#N` tokens**, **660 lines are BuildKit step lines**. `#5604` is an npm\npostinstall regression. Cross-referenced against `/workspace/push_notes_v18.sh` header\nlines 12–16 (rules #7,#8,#28,#34/#47,#37,#38,#39/#45,#41,#53,#54,#55,#57). Definitions\nare not in this corpus; prose `Rule #N` totals 15 lines (#54×6, #53×3, #39×3, #28×3).\n\n## 3. JEV references\n\n**In notes (`.txt`):** 10 files / 1,341 lines; `JEV`×693, `jev-review`×321,\n`jev-guard`×250, `Jev`×159, plus `jev-latest`×9, `jev-repo`×6, `jev-classifier`×6,\n`jev-deepseek`×4. **In `/workspace`** (excluding .git/node_modules/notes/data/logs):\n128 files / 2,328 lines. Recurring theme: Jev is installed/string-matched but never\nfunctionally proven.\n\n## 4. Current state\n\n`opencode-web` block (docker-compose.yml 45–71): image `opencode-deepseek-jev:robust`,\nentrypoint `/workspace/docker/web-entrypoint.sh`, port `4096:4096`, volumes `..:/workspace`\nand `../data/opencode:/home/node/.local/share/opencode`, `env_file ../.env.local`,\n`OPENCODE_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS=true`, `restart: unless-stopped`, `no-new-privileges`,\n`cap_drop: ALL` with CHOWN/SETUID/SETGID. The tracked web block has **no notes mount**;\nit comes only from the untracked `docker-compose.override.yml`.\n\n`web-entrypoint.sh`: writes `auth.json` via Node one-liner, symlinks `/workspace` to\n`/home/node/workspace`, then `exec opencode web --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096`.\n\nSession count via `node --experimental-sqlite` (sqlite3/python3 absent):\nsession=20, message=148, part=712, project=2, event=2653.\n\n## 5. Sidebar streaming\n\n**Yes — a processing session is visible in the sidebar.** SPA subscribes to `/api/event`\n(SSE); `session.created` then `session.updated` / `message.updated` keep the entry in\nsync. Not `/api/session/active`. Live evidence from `event` table: session.created=20,\nsession.updated=206, message.updated=541, message.part.updated=1886, including the\ncurrent audit session. Caveat: proves the event stream, not the DOM render.\n\n## 6. Operator next steps\n\n1. Track the notes mount in docker-compose.yml.\n2. Recover/version the canonical rules document.\n3. Bake in sqlite3/python3 or standardize on Node.\n4. Add test-sidebar-streaming.sh regression test.\n5. Tame drift/secrets: 194 git entries (171 untracked), rotate keys.\n"}],"repositoryContext":"Container: opencode-deepseek-web, user node, Node v22.23.2. /workspace/notes is read-only and contains 41 files (12 txt, 28 png, 1 py). sqlite3 and python3 are NOT installed; node --experimental-sqlite is the only DB access. Tracked docker/docker-compose.yml exposes an opencode-web service with no notes volume; the notes mount exists only in untracked docker/docker-compose.override.yml. opencode.json wires provider deepseek/deepseek-flash, plugin jev-guard, skills /opt/jev-review/skills, MCP server jev-review. Dockerfile installs jev-guard@0.3.1 and clones/je builds NiazMorshed2007/jev-review pinned at 3fb6042e. Previous logs/sidebar-audit.md existed (same task, earlier run) and was overwritten. Live DB counts move between reads; the report labels them as a moving target."} failed
